<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bannockburn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1314">1314</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bannockburn was fought on 23–24 June 1314 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, between the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a> and a much larger English army under Edward II. Edward's attempt to relieve Stirling Castle ended in a heavy English defeat on the boggy ground by the Bannock Burn. The victory secured Bruce's kingship, though the war went on until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-edinburgh-northampton">Treaty of Edinburgh–Northampton</a> recognised Scottish independence in 1328.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bannockburn.jpg" alt="Battle of Bannockburn" width="320" height="501" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Bannockburn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
